First Author: Kim
Title: An integrated clinical-histopathologic prediction model for cardiac allograft rejection: Translating machine learning into clinical risk frameworks
Source number: 64

Very short summary: This retrospective single-center study included 484 adult heart transplant recipients contributing 1,188 outpatient endomyocardial-biopsy encounters during the first 6 months after transplantation. An XGBoost model integrating longitudinal clinical data with quantitative biopsy morphologic features achieved a held-out test AUROC of 0.86 and AUPRC of 0.74 for future cardiac allograft rejection within 6 weeks; the authors subsequently translated influential predictors into the interpretable Integrated Rejection Risk Index.

