	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Patients were required to have at least 90% completeness of routinely collected clinical variables, and residual missingness was handled using multiple imputation by chained equations. The cohort was deliberately enriched for future-rejection patients, 26.9% versus a 15.1% institutional incidence, “to mitigate class imbalance.” Longitudinal predictors were constructed using time bins, change-from-baseline, change-from-prior-encounter, and rate-of-change features. Figure 2 reports 954 training encounters and 234 held-out test encounters; all splitting was performed at patient level. Code availability was not reported.

