	•	Decision Curve Analysis (DCA) Reported: No
	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The primary feasibility outcome was future cardiac allograft rejection occurring more than 7 days and no more than 42 days after a CAR-free outpatient encounter. CAR included ISHLT cellular rejection greater than 1R, pAMR greater than 0, or clinically evident rejection. On the held-out test set of 234 encounters, the integrated longitudinal clinical-morphologic XGBoost model achieved AUROC 0.86, AUPRC 0.74, macro F1 0.83, sensitivity 0.72, specificity 0.94, PPV 0.74, and NPV 0.94. Numeric 95% confidence bounds for AUROC and accuracy were not reported. Formal calibration analysis and DCA were not reported.

